# Vouch — Backend Agent Rules

Read `context/1-project-overview.md` through `context/7-units.md` before writing any code. Full detail lives there; this file is the always-loaded summary.

## Non-negotiable
* Work only on the backend Trust Profile API.
* Keep frontend and UI changes out of this backend change.
* Migrations are additive only. Never modify an applied migration or delete production data.
* Every owner endpoint uses the existing Supabase JWT middleware and validates ownership.
* Public profile and confirmation endpoints expose only explicitly selected fields; never expose email, Supabase user IDs, customer names, confirmation tokens, private notes, or other internal data.
* Evidence status is `SELF_REPORTED` or `CUSTOMER_CONFIRMED`; confirmation state is pending, confirmed, declined, or expired. See `context/3-api-contract.md`.
* Keep the backend limited to profiles, evidence, and customer confirmations.

## Working style
* Follow the requested scope and existing backend patterns.
* Document every new endpoint, model, or migration in `backend/TRUST_PROFILE_API.md` as you build it.
* Before every push: `git diff --check`, `git status --short`, and the relevant build/test.
